&lt;div class="alert alert-tip"&gt;
	&lt;div class="alert-header"&gt;
		
		

	&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" height="20px" viewBox="0 -960 960 960" width="20px"&gt;&lt;path d="M407.74-240Q378-240 357-261.15 336-282.3 336-312v-67q-57-37.3-88.5-95.65Q216-533 216-600q0-110.31 76.78-187.16 76.78-76.84 187-76.84T667-787.16q77 76.85 77 187.16 0 66.82-31.5 125.41T624-379v67q0 29.7-21.18 50.85Q581.65-240 551.91-240H407.74Zm.26-72h144v-86q0-9.29 4-17.64 4-8.36 12-12.92l17-10.93q41-25.51 64-68.69 23-43.18 23-91.82 0-79.68-56.23-135.84-56.22-56.16-136-56.16Q400-792 344-735.84 288-679.68 288-600q0 48.64 23 91.82 23 43.18 64 68.69l17 10.93q8 4.56 12 12.92 4 8.35 4 17.64v86ZM396-96q-15.3 0-25.65-10.29Q360-116.58 360-131.79t10.35-25.71Q380.7-168 396-168h168q15.3 0 25.65 10.29Q600-147.42 600-132.21t-10.35 25.71Q579.3-96 564-96H396Zm84-504Z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;


		&lt;span&gt;
		
			Tip
		
		&lt;/span&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;div class="alert-body"&gt;
		&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We use &lt;a href="https://serde.rs/#data-structures" target="_blank" &gt;Serde&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;Serialize&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Deserialize&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; derive macros to parse Rust structs directly from a JSON stream and to generate a JSON stream from Rust structs. This process eliminates the need of maintaining intermediate types, and maximizing the processing efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third-party crates support Serde serialization and deserialization through feature flags.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="add-serde-support"&gt;Add Serde Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run following &lt;code&gt;cargo add&lt;/code&gt; commands from the &lt;code&gt;book_service&lt;/code&gt; folder.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>